],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-07-22T17:47:36Z","updated_at":"2026-07-22T19:32:28Z","closed_at":"2026-07-22T19:31:01Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7.1 stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - macOS Tahoe (26.5.2) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M5 (Apple9) - Apple M5 (10 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\ngit stashing after moving a file to a new folder leaves the file in both positions. Reloading the project and deleting the .godot folders do not fix this bug. Cloning again from a remote repository does not fix this either. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start an empty project with default settings\n2. Open the project folder, run ```git init``` and ```git add --all```, and commit with ```git commit -m \"initial commit\"```.\n3. Move the file icon.svg using either `mv` or dragging it within the editor filesystem. \n4. Run `git stash`.\n5. The file will now be located in both locations, and reloading and deleting project.godot and .godot folders do not solve this bug.\n\n<img width=\"428\" height=\"489\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23178228-315d-431a-937b-764057f9b7aa\" />\n\n<img width=\"138\" height=\"141\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/891e7507-c1fb-4b4d-b562-47d7e52258fa\" />\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bug-test-proj.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30278901/bug-test-proj.zip)\n\n\n\nSorry if I'm doing this incorrectly, I'm new to contributing to open source. Thanks!","closed_by":{"login":"HonestlyFranklySpeaking","id":213770735,"node_id":"U_kgDODL3